# Copy to /etc/tvlens/runtime.env. Explicitly set YOUR server's Tailscale IP.
# Never use 0.0.0.0 for a private-only installation.
TVLENS_BIND=127.0.0.1
TVLENS_PORT=8787

# Session titles ("Session du 18 oct. 2026, 10:33") are written in the server's time zone. A server
# in UTC shows the household's sessions hours off: set the household's zone.
# TZ=Europe/Paris

# Optional: chat reasoning effort; default low, model must support chosen value.
# TVLENS_CHAT_REASONING_EFFORT=max

# Codex confinement. Nothing to set for the default ("enforce"), and the default REFUSES every Codex
# connection (chat, surveillance, manual check, passage description, recap) unless Codex confirms
# the two settings that forbid sub-agent creation: accepted by this binary (`codex features list -c
# <key>`), passed at launch and read back by config/read. A Codex that does not know them, cannot be
# asked, or does not state them means NO Codex answer at all on this server until Codex is upgraded.
# Nothing was measured on Linux. Before putting this server in service (SECURITY.md, "Avant tout
# déploiement"): note `codex --version`, then replay
#   node scripts/probe-confinement.cjs --out <new dir> --steps r --max-turns 0     (no model turn)
# and the full probe. The refusal message names the installed version and the version measured.
# "strict" also refuses a thread whose confinement the App Server does not state (another version):
# TVLENS_CODEX_CONFINEMENT=strict
# DIAGNOSTIC MODE, NOT CONFINED. "report" refuses nothing (neither an unconfirmed sub-agent block nor
# a thread the App Server contradicts) and writes a journal line at every connection. It must be set
# explicitly, here and nowhere else; a server left in this mode runs not confined. Unset after use:
# TVLENS_CODEX_CONFINEMENT=report
# Fallbacks, each one removes a control. Use only to diagnose a regression, then unset:
# TVLENS_CODEX_ITEM_GUARD=legacy     # former deny-list of four item types instead of the allow-list;
#                                    # also stops closing the process when a sub-agent shows (its
#                                    # thread, or an item reporting it). The launch settings that
#                                    # forbid sub-agent creation are still passed and required.
# TVLENS_CODEX_REAL_HOME=1           # Codex children keep the service HOME instead of an empty one
# TVLENS_COMPANION_PROMPT=legacy     # former companion prompt
